  message: "GOVERNANCE APPROVAL REQUESTED — do not implement until approved. This guard touches scripts/auto-pr and scripts/merge-pr (governance files), so per the AGENTS.md governance approval workflow it is filed needs_human_review with no preemptive PR. Two things to decide before implementation: (1) Auto-close vs. hard-warn vs. the hybrid (hard-warn always + auto-close only on an explicit evidence-carrying syntax) — my recommendation is the hybrid, because pure auto-close bypasses the closure-evidence discipline (G10/WI-dafun) for behavioral items. (2) Whether the guard lives in auto-pr only, merge-pr only, or both (and whether the shared logic belongs in scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh, also governance). Motivation and full evidence are in the description: the inert 'Closes …' commit-message idiom has already left ≥3 items (WI-dafun, WI-kafar, WI-himoj, +WI-niluv) stale despite merged code — a process gap, not a sync/durability failure. Please reply with approval + your decision on (1) and (2), or redirect."  # 57c8
